-- title:
--   Idèle classes modulo norms as ray classes modulo the norm-ray subgroup
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, let $\mathfrak f$ be a nonzero ideal of $\mathcal O_K$, and let $\mathrm{Nrm}$ be a group homomorphism from the units of the adèle ring of $L$ to the units of the adèle ring of $K$, subject to three hypotheses. First, $\mathrm{Nrm}$ carries adjuster pairs to adjuster pairs: whenever $u$ and $\alpha \in L^\times$ satisfy [`HeckeCharacter.IsAdjuster`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ArtinCoreCTM.html#L246) at the extended modulus $\mathfrak f\mathcal O_L$ — that is, at each prime $w \mid \mathfrak f\mathcal O_L$ the $w$-component of $u\alpha^{-1}$ is a unit congruent to $1$ modulo $w^{n_w}$ (its valuation is $1$ and the valuation of the component minus $1$ is at most $\exp(-n_w)$, $n_w$ the multiplicity of $w$ in $\mathfrak f\mathcal O_L$), and $u\alpha^{-1}$ is positive at every real embedding — then $\mathrm{Nrm}(u)$ and $N_{L/K}(\alpha)$ are adjusters at level $\mathfrak f$. Second, the content of $\mathrm{Nrm}(u)$ (the fractional ideal $\prod_v v^{\mathrm{ord}_v}$ of the finite part, `fadContentHom` of `projFin`) is the relative ideal norm [`HeckeCharacter.fracRelNormUnit`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ArtinCoreCTM.html#L27) of the content of $u$. Third, every element of [`LanglandsTunnell.P2.Artin.unitIdeles K 𝔣`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ArtinCoreCTM.html#L343) — adèle units all of whose finite components are units, congruent to $1$ modulo $v^{n_v}$ at each $v \mid \mathfrak f$, and positive at each real embedding — lies in the range of $\mathrm{Nrm}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a group isomorphism $\varphi$ from the quotient of the idèle units of $K$ by the subgroup generated by the diagonal image of $K^\times$ together with the range of $\mathrm{Nrm}$, onto the quotient of the group of invertible fractional ideals with $v$-multiplicity $0$ at every $v \mid \mathfrak f$ by [`LanglandsTunnell.P2.Artin.normRaySubgroup K L 𝔣`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ArtinCoreCTM.html#L320), the join of the subgroup generated by `narrowRaySet K 𝔣` (restricted to that group) with the range of the relative norm [`HeckeCharacter.relNormCTM K L 𝔣`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ArtinCoreCTM.html#L69) on ideals coprime to $\mathfrak f\mathcal O_L$; moreover $\varphi$ is explicit on classes of $1$-adjusted idèles: for every $u$ which is an adjuster at level $\mathfrak f$ with $\alpha = 1$ and whose content is coprime to $\mathfrak f$, $\varphi$ sends the class of $u$ to the class of that content.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the idelic and the ideal-theoretic (ray class) formulations of class field theory, in the relative form needed when the modulus is deep enough that the congruence unit idèles are norms, here abstracted as the third hypothesis. It is used in the construction of the idelic Artin map, in [`NumberField.exists_idelicArtinMap_ker_eq_and_surjective_and_eq_finprod_artinFrob_of_dvd_twentyFour`](thm.html#NumberField.exists_idelicArtinMap_ker_eq_and_surjective_and_eq_finprod_artinFrob_of_dvd_twentyFour) and in [`NumberField.exists_idelicArtinMap_ker_eq_and_surjective_and_eq_finprod_artinFrob_of_isAdmissibleModulusOfDegree_finrank`](thm.html#NumberField.exists_idelicArtinMap_ker_eq_and_surjective_and_eq_finprod_artinFrob_of_isAdmissibleModulusOfDegree_finrank).
